  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212614/assets/a7fb89105bc5a11837ed0f416b2327d88202e8e782fa4c114ac47b3d5d15421c.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?",
  "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(7,-2).$ So, our actual value is $y=-2.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=7$ has the $y$-coordinate $-4.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=-4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212614/assets/92a26b8ab019879dec3208878f6a0604c0616776b09e3f8fa916fcab72df3a73.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-2-(-4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
